title: StructureMenu
tags: structure interaction
---
// The ONE parameterized building-interaction node. The caller sets $structureId
// (DialogueService.PlayStructure); everything below is data-driven from that id —
// the portrait (Portraits/<id>), the name/level/yield, and the upgrade cost — so a
// building can only ever surface its OWN domain (no out-of-domain options).
//   Buy / Sell  = open the real stocked ShopPanel (GearCatalog weapons/armor +
//                 VillageInventory) via the OpenShop vendor verb, scoped to this
//                 building's $structureId so the panel shows the right flavour.
//   Upgrade     = the live option (levels + perks via the economy backend).
//   Talk        = narrative/questline seed (e.g. the Forge's "forgotten hammer").
// NOTE: only ONE command runs at node entry on purpose. Two back-to-back synchronous
// commands (<<portrait>> then <<structure_status>>) tripped a Yarn v3 re-entrancy bug —
// each synchronous command's OnCommandReceivedAsync calls Dialogue.Continue(), which
// pumps the VM into the NEXT command inline, and the nested SignalContentComplete then
// throws "can only be called when a command is being dispatched", aborting the whole
// dialogue (Talk did nothing). structure_status now ALSO forces the portrait, so the
// node opens with a single command and the prologue can't re-enter itself.
<<structure_status $structureId>>

{$structureName}: Need something?

-> Upgrade — {$upgradeCostText} <<if $structureCanUpgrade>>
    <<structure_upgrade $structureId>>
    {$structureName}: {$upgradeResult}
-> Buy <<if $structureCanShop>>
    {$structureName}: Take a look at what I have.
    <<OpenShop $structureId>>
-> Sell <<if $structureCanShop>>
    {$structureName}: Show me what you'd part with.
    <<OpenShop $structureId>>
-> Talk
    <<structure_talk $structureId>>
    {$structureName}: Always work to be done around here. Stick around and I might have a task for you.
-> Leave
    {$structureName}: Safe travels.
===

title: PetHouse
tags: structure interaction pet
---
// The Echo Hollow's OWN flow: "visit the hollow to attune and select an echo."
// (WO-338 rebrand: pet→Echo, Pet House→Echo Hollow, adopt→attune, NPC = Echo Warden.
//  INTERNAL ids unchanged — node title "PetHouse", structureId "pet-house", and the
//  echo species ids "ice-wolf"/"flame-pup"/"aether-sprite" are keyed by code; only the
//  player-facing TEXT is rebranded.)
// The player attunes an echo SPECIES via Yarn options; <<spawn_named_pet>> deploys the
// chosen species through the self-healed PetDeployer (DialogueCommandBridge).
// DialogueService.PlayStructure("pet-house", …) routes here (not the generic StructureMenu).
//
// The opening line carries #lastline so it renders inside the options view (alongside
// the choices) instead of the standalone line panel — see WO-337: the standalone line
// panel would otherwise stay on screen UNDER the option list and read as overlapping text.
//
// TODO: free-text echo NAMING — Yarn options can't capture typed text, so the echo
// takes its catalog name for now (Aether Sprite / Flame Pup / Ice Wolf). A code-built
// name-entry UI (cf. PetIntroduction) would write GameState.PetName before deploy.
<<portrait Portraits/pet-house>>
// STATEFUL gate (pet re-select fix): each attune option is wrapped in
// <<if not pet_owned("<species>")>> so an echo the player has ALREADY bonded no
// longer appears as a selectable unlock. pet_owned(id) is a Yarn function
// registered in DialogueCommandBridge, backed by PetAcquisitionService.Owns (the
// canonical roster) with a GameState.StarterPetId fallback for legacy saves. The
// <<spawn_named_pet>> command is ALSO idempotent (Acquire no-ops on an owned
// species) so the grant can never double-fire. When an echo is already bonded the
// Warden offers a "they already walk with you" line instead of re-attuning.
Echo Warden: Welcome to the Echo Hollow. The echoes here seek a bond. Choose one — they will fight at your side, guard Elarion, and return to you always. #lastline

-> A frost-warden — the Ice Wolf. Steady and tough. <<if not pet_owned("ice-wolf")>>
    <<spawn_named_pet "ice-wolf">>
    Echo Warden: The Ice Wolf is attuned to you. It will chill any foe that nears the Heart.
-> The Ice Wolf already walks with you. <<if pet_owned("ice-wolf")>>
    Echo Warden: The Ice Wolf is already bonded to you — it answers your call when you need it.
-> A hearth-hound — the Flame Pup. Fierce and fast. <<if not pet_owned("flame-pup")>>
    <<spawn_named_pet "flame-pup">>
    Echo Warden: The Flame Pup answers your call. Its embers will scorch the enemy.
-> The Flame Pup already walks with you. <<if pet_owned("flame-pup")>>
    Echo Warden: The Flame Pup is already bonded to you — its embers are yours to command.
-> A heart-ward — the Aether Sprite. Quick and arcane. <<if not pet_owned("aether-sprite")>>
    <<spawn_named_pet "aether-sprite">>
    Echo Warden: The Aether Sprite flits to your side. It will ward the Heart with arcane light.
-> The Aether Sprite already walks with you. <<if pet_owned("aether-sprite")>>
    Echo Warden: The Aether Sprite is already bonded to you — its arcane light is ever at your side.
-> Not yet — I will return.
    Echo Warden: The hollow is always open when you are ready.
===
